== S1 odd-function floor law ==
  S1 law holds for ['x', 'x^3', 'x^5', 'x^3+x', '3x', 'x^7-5x^3+x', 'x^3-100x (negative values)', '-7x^9+x (negative values)'], all 2 <= n <= 400 (Python floor is the true floor for negative values)
  S1 n=1: both sides 0 (degenerate, consistent; the lane states n >= 2)
  S1 generic odd functions Z -> Z with f(n-k) = -f(k) (mod n) only (random lifts): law holds 2 <= n < 80
  S1 n=6, f=x^3: pairs (1,1,5),(2,2,4), fixed residue 3; n=12 fixed residue 0; n=4 fixed residue 0
  S1 even f: n=2 holds for all four; minimal failures {'x^2': (3, 1, '2/3'), 'x^4': (3, 5, '14/3'), 'x^2+x': (3, 2, '13/6'), '2 (const)': (3, 0, '1/3')}
