== S2 fixed layer Z_{x^e}(n) = n/n_e - 1, squarefree truth sets ==
  S2 Z_{x^e}(n) = n/n_e - 1 for 1 <= e <= 9, 2 <= n <= 2000 (direct count via pow(k,e,n))
  S2 truth set of (1) on [2,2000] = squarefree, 1214 values
  S2 table (n, floor sum, RHS(1), Z_3) confirmed at n = 4, 8, 9, 12, 36; deviation = Z_3/2
  S2 odd e = 3,5,7,9: zero-defect identity on [2,1200] iff squarefree; e = 1 holds for all n
  S2 Z_7(n) = n/rad(n) - 1 on [2,300) fails only at n = 256: Z_7(256) = 63, 256/rad(256) - 1 = 127
     CORRECTION: the lane script printed the hard-coded literal '256/rad-1 = 255' and the note repeated 255; rad(256) = 2 so the true value is 127 (256 = 2^8, n_7 = 2^2 = 4, Z_7 = 64 - 1 = 63)
  S2 #squarefree <= 10^6 = 607926 by Moebius sum (matches the lane's sieve count)
[t=9.2s]

